#: src/ui/state.md:228
msgid "[Events](events.md) — Click, hover, keyboard events"
msgstr "[Eventos](events.md) — Eventos de clic, hover y teclado"

#: src/ui/events.md:3
msgid ""
"Perry widgets support native event handlers for user interaction. Every "
"snippet below is excerpted from [`docs/examples/ui/events/snippets.ts`]"
"(../../examples/ui/events/snippets.ts) — CI compiles and runs it on every "
"PR, so the API drawn here is the API the runtime exposes."
msgstr ""
"Los widgets de Perry admiten manejadores de eventos nativos para la "
"interacción del usuario. Cada fragmento a continuación está extraído de "
"[`docs/examples/ui/events/snippets.ts`](../../examples/ui/events/"
"snippets.ts) — CI lo compila y ejecuta en cada PR, por lo que la API "
"mostrada aquí es la API que expone el runtime."

#: src/ui/events.md:9
msgid ""
"Event handlers are registered as **free functions** that take the widget "
"handle as the first argument. The widget handle itself is opaque (`number` "
"at the type level); perry's API is function-first throughout."
msgstr ""
"Los manejadores de eventos se registran como **funciones libres** que "
"reciben el handle del widget como primer argumento. El handle del widget en "
"sí es opaco (`number` a nivel de tipo); la API de perry es de función-"
"primero en todo momento."

#: src/ui/events.md:13 src/testing/geisterhand.md:100
msgid "onClick"
msgstr "onClick"

#: src/ui/events.md:15
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"const greet = Button(\"Click me\", () => {\n"
"    log.set(\"Button clicked\")\n"
"})\n"
"\n"
"// Or attach a click handler to a non-button widget after creation:\n"
"const label = Text(\"Clickable text\")\n"
"widgetSetOnClick(label, () => {\n"
"    log.set(\"Text clicked\")\n"
"})\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"const greet = Button(\"Click me\", () => {\n"
"    log.set(\"Button clicked\")\n"
"})\n"
"\n"
"// Or attach a click handler to a non-button widget after creation:\n"
"const label = Text(\"Clickable text\")\n"
"widgetSetOnClick(label, () => {\n"
"    log.set(\"Text clicked\")\n"
"})\n"
"```"

#: src/ui/events.md:27 src/testing/geisterhand.md:103
msgid "onHover"
msgstr "onHover"

#: src/ui/events.md:29
msgid "Triggered when the cursor enters the widget."
msgstr "Se dispara cuando el cursor entra en el widget."

#: src/ui/events.md:31
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"const hoverBtn = Button(\"Hover me\", () => {})\n"
"widgetSetOnHover(hoverBtn, () => {\n"
"    log.set(\"hovered\")\n"
"})\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"const hoverBtn = Button(\"Hover me\", () => {})\n"
"widgetSetOnHover(hoverBtn, () => {\n"
"    log.set(\"hovered\")\n"
"})\n"
"```"

#: src/ui/events.md:38
msgid ""
"**Note**: Hover events are available on macOS, Windows, Linux, and Web. iOS "
"and Android use touch interactions instead. The callback fires once on "
"enter; if you need a \"left\" event you'll have to track it yourself."
msgstr ""
"**Nota**: Los eventos hover están disponibles en macOS, Windows, Linux y "
"Web. iOS y Android usan interacciones táctiles en su lugar. El callback se "
"dispara una vez al entrar; si necesita un evento de \"salida\" deberá "
"rastrearlo usted mismo."

