msgid "`wear` and `wear-os` are accepted as aliases for `wearos`."
msgstr "`wear` y `wear-os` se aceptan como alias para `wearos`."

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:97
msgid ""
"Identical to [Android](android.md) — the same `perry/ui` widgets map to the "
"same Android `View` classes (`Text` → `TextView`, `VStack` → vertical "
"`LinearLayout`, `Button` → `Button`, `ScrollView` → `ScrollView`, and so "
"on). No Wear-specific widget API is required: an Android UI tree renders "
"directly on a watch."
msgstr ""
"Idéntica a [Android](android.md) — los mismos widgets `perry/ui` se asignan "
"a las mismas clases Android `View` (`Text` → `TextView`, `VStack` → vertical "
"`LinearLayout`, `Button` → `Button`, `ScrollView` → `ScrollView`, y así "
"sucesivamente). No se requiere una API de widget específica para el "
"desgaste: un árbol de interfaz de usuario Android renderiza directamente en "
"un reloj."

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:102
msgid ""
"The `androidx.wear` dependency in the overlay brings in `BoxInsetLayout` and "
"swipe-to-dismiss so round screens and the back gesture behave like a native "
"Wear app."
msgstr ""
"La dependencia de `androidx.wear` en la superposición trae `BoxInsetLayout` "
"y deslizarse para deshacerse de las pantallas redondas y el gesto de espalda "
"se comportan como una aplicación nativa Wear."

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:108
msgid ""
"A Wear OS app uses the same `App({...})` entry point as every other Perry UI "
"target:"
msgstr ""
"Una aplicación Wear OS utiliza el mismo punto de entrada `App({...})` que "
"cualquier otro objetivo de interfaz de usuario Perry:"

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:111
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"import { App, Text, VStack, Button, State } from \"perry/ui\"\n"
"\n"
"const count = State(0)\n"
"\n"
"App({\n"
"    title: \"My Watch App\",\n"
"    width: 200,\n"
"    height: 200,\n"
"    body: VStack(8, [\n"
"        Text(\"Hello, Wear OS!\"),\n"
"        Text(`Taps: ${count.value}`),\n"
"        Button(\"Tap me\", () => count.set(count.value + 1)),\n"
"    ]),\n"
"})\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"import { App, Text, VStack, Button, State } from \"perry/ui\"\n"
"\n"
"const count = State(0)\n"
"\n"
"App({\n"
"    title: \"My Watch App\",\n"
"    width: 200,\n"
"    height: 200,\n"
"    body: VStack(8, [\n"
"        Text(\"Hello, Wear OS!\"),\n"
"        Text(`Taps: ${count.value}`),\n"
"        Button(\"Tap me\", () => count.set(count.value + 1)),\n"
"    ]),\n"
"})\n"
"```"

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:128
msgid ""
"Under the hood this is the Android lifecycle: `PerryActivity` loads "
"`libperry_app.so`, calls into your compiled `main()` over JNI, and the "
"`perry/ui` tree is realized as Android `View`s on the watch."
msgstr ""
"Bajo el capó está el ciclo de vida Android: `PerryActivity` carga "
"`libperry_app.so`, llama a su compilado `main()` sobre JNI, y el árbol "
"`perry/ui` se realiza como Android `View` en el reloj."

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:134
msgid "Reactive state works exactly as on Android and the other platforms:"
msgstr ""
"El estado reactivo funciona exactamente como en Android y las otras "
"plataformas:"

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:154
msgid ""
"Because the runtime target triple is `aarch64-linux-android`, a Wear OS app "
"reports the **Android** platform number — `__platform__ === 2`:"
msgstr ""
"Debido a que el objetivo de tiempo de ejecución triple es `aarch64-linux-"
"android`, una aplicación Wear OS informa de la **Android** número de "
"plataforma — `__platform__ === 2`:"

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:180
msgid ""
"There is intentionally no separate Wear OS platform constant: at runtime a "
"Wear app _is_ an Android app. Branch on screen size at runtime if you need "
"watch-specific layout."
msgstr ""
"No existe intencionadamente ninguna constante de plataforma Wear OS "
"separada: en tiempo de ejecución una aplicación Wear _is_ una aplicación "
"Android. Rama en tamaño de pantalla en tiempo de ejecución si necesita "
"diseño específico de reloj."

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:186
msgid ""
"Wear OS reuses the `[android]` section of `perry.toml` (bundle id, etc.):"
msgstr ""
"Wear OS reutiliza la sección `[android]` de `perry.toml` (id. de grupo, "
"etc.):"

