#: src/stdlib/fs.md:3
msgid ""
"Perry implements Node.js file system APIs for reading, writing, and managing "
"files."
msgstr ""
"Perry implementa las APIs del sistema de archivos de Node.js para leer, "
"escribir y gestionar archivos."

#: src/stdlib/fs.md:5
msgid "Reading Files"
msgstr "Lectura de Archivos"

#: src/stdlib/fs.md:7
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"const configPath = join(scratch, \"config.json\")\n"
"const content = readFileSync(configPath, \"utf-8\")\n"
"console.log(content)\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"const configPath = join(scratch, \"config.json\")\n"
"const content = readFileSync(configPath, \"utf-8\")\n"
"console.log(content)\n"
"```"

#: src/stdlib/fs.md:13
msgid "Binary File Reading"
msgstr "Lectura de Archivos Binarios"

#: src/stdlib/fs.md:15
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"const imagePath = join(scratch, \"image.png\")\n"
"const buffer = fs.readFileBuffer(imagePath)\n"
"console.log(`Read ${buffer.length} bytes`)\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"const imagePath = join(scratch, \"image.png\")\n"
"const buffer = fs.readFileBuffer(imagePath)\n"
"console.log(`Read ${buffer.length} bytes`)\n"
"```"

#: src/stdlib/fs.md:21
msgid ""
"`readFileBuffer` reads files as binary data (uses `fs::read()` internally, "
"not `read_to_string()`)."
msgstr ""
"`readFileBuffer` lee archivos como datos binarios (usa `fs::read()` "
"internamente, no `read_to_string()`)."

#: src/stdlib/fs.md:23
msgid "Writing Files"
msgstr "Escritura de Archivos"

#: src/stdlib/fs.md:25
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"const outputPath = join(scratch, \"output.txt\")\n"
"const dataPath = join(scratch, \"data.json\")\n"
"writeFileSync(outputPath, \"Hello, World!\")\n"
"writeFileSync(dataPath, JSON.stringify({ key: \"value\" }, null, 2))\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"const outputPath = join(scratch, \"output.txt\")\n"
"const dataPath = join(scratch, \"data.json\")\n"
"writeFileSync(outputPath, \"Hello, World!\")\n"
"writeFileSync(dataPath, JSON.stringify({ key: \"value\" }, null, 2))\n"
"```"

#: src/stdlib/fs.md:32
msgid "File Information"
msgstr "Información de Archivos"

#: src/stdlib/fs.md:41
msgid "Directory Operations"
msgstr "Operaciones de Directorio"

#: src/stdlib/fs.md:43
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"// Create directory\n"
"const outDir = join(scratch, \"output\")\n"
"if (!existsSync(outDir)) mkdirSync(outDir)\n"
"\n"
"// Read directory contents\n"
"const files = readdirSync(scratch)\n"
"for (const file of files) {\n"
"    console.log(file)\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"// Remove an empty directory\n"
"rmdirSync(outDir)\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"// Create directory\n"
"const outDir = join(scratch, \"output\")\n"
"if (!existsSync(outDir)) mkdirSync(outDir)\n"
"\n"
"// Read directory contents\n"
"const files = readdirSync(scratch)\n"
"for (const file of files) {\n"
"    console.log(file)\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"// Remove an empty directory\n"
"rmdirSync(outDir)\n"
"```"

#: src/stdlib/fs.md:58
msgid ""
"For recursive removal Perry exposes `rmRecursive` (a thin wrapper around "
"`std::fs::remove_dir_all`). Wired via [\\#193](https://github.com/PerryTS/"
"perry/issues/193) through `js_fs_rm_recursive` in the LLVM backend."
msgstr ""
"Para eliminación recursiva Perry expone `rmRecursive` (un thin wrapper sobre "
"`std::fs::remove_dir_all`). Conectado vía [\\#193](https://github.com/"
"PerryTS/perry/issues/193) a través de `js_fs_rm_recursive` en el backend "
"LLVM."

#: src/stdlib/fs.md:63
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"import { rmRecursive } from \"fs\";\n"
"rmRecursive(\"output\"); // Recursive remove; returns 1 on success, 0 on "
"failure.\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"import { rmRecursive } from \"fs\";\n"
"rmRecursive(\"output\"); // Recursive remove; returns 1 on success, 0 on "
"failure.\n"
"```"

#: src/stdlib/fs.md:68
msgid "Path Utilities"
msgstr "Utilidades de Rutas"

#: src/stdlib/fs.md:70
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"const dir = dirname(configPath)\n"
"const cfgPath = join(dir, \"config.json\")\n"
"const name = basename(cfgPath)        // \"config.json\"\n"
"const abs = resolve(\"relative/path\")  // Absolute path\n"
"console.log(`${name} ${abs.length > 0}`)\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"const dir = dirname(configPath)\n"
"const cfgPath = join(dir, \"config.json\")\n"
"const name = basename(cfgPath)        // \"config.json\"\n"
"const abs = resolve(\"relative/path\")  // Absolute path\n"
"console.log(`${name} ${abs.length > 0}`)\n"
"```"

#: src/stdlib/fs.md:78
msgid ""
"For `import.meta.url` → filesystem path conversion, use `fileURLToPath` from "
"the `url` module:"
msgstr ""
"Para la conversión de `import.meta.url` a ruta del sistema de archivos, usa "
"`fileURLToPath` del módulo `url`:"

#: src/stdlib/fs.md:81
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"import { fileURLToPath } from \"url\";\n"
"import { dirname } from \"path\";\n"
"\n"
"const dir = dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"import { fileURLToPath } from \"url\";\n"
"import { dirname } from \"path\";\n"
"\n"
"const dir = dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\n"
"```"

#: src/stdlib/fs.md:90
msgid ""
"`fs` numeric file descriptors and `fs.promises.FileHandle` objects are "
"thread-affine across `perry/thread`. Passing a numeric fd into `spawn` or "
"`parallelMap` copies only the number; the receiving thread has its own fd "
"registry, so operations fail with `EBADF`. Passing a `FileHandle` produces a "
"detached handle with `fd === -1`."
msgstr ""
"Los descriptores de archivo numéricos de `fs` y los objetos "
"`fs.promises.FileHandle` son thread-affine en `perry/thread`. Pasar un fd "
"numérico a `spawn` o `parallelMap` copia solo el número; el hilo receptor "
"tiene su propio registro de fds, por lo que las operaciones fallan con "
"`EBADF`. Pasar un `FileHandle` produce un handle desvinculado con `fd === "
"-1`."

#: src/stdlib/fs.md:96
msgid ""
"Pass file paths across thread boundaries and reopen files inside the worker."
msgstr ""
"Pasa rutas de archivo entre límites de hilo y reabre los archivos dentro del "
"worker."

