#: src/container/overview.md:76
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"import {\n"
"  setBackend, setBackends, getBackend, getBackendPriority,\n"
"  getAvailableBackends, selectBackendFor, up,\n"
"} from 'perry/container';\n"
"\n"
"// (3a) Pin a specific backend for everything in this process.\n"
"await setBackend('docker');\n"
"\n"
"// (3b) Or — try a list in user-defined priority order (first\n"
"//      available wins). Useful for \"prefer rootless, fall back to\n"
"//      docker\" patterns and CI matrix lanes.\n"
"await setBackends(['podman', 'docker']);\n"
"\n"
"// (4) Or — let Perry pick the best backend FOR THIS SPEC.\n"
"//     Spec uses privileged: true → returns \"docker\" / \"podman\" (not "
"apple).\n"
"//     Trivial spec on macOS → returns \"apple/container\".\n"
"const best = JSON.parse(selectBackendFor(JSON.stringify(spec))) as string;\n"
"await setBackend(best);\n"
"await up(spec);\n"
"\n"
"// Diagnostics — which backends does Perry know about, and which are\n"
"// actually installed on this host?\n"
"console.log(getBackend());                                          // "
"\"docker\" (active)\n"
"console.log(JSON.parse(getBackendPriority()));                      // "
"[\"apple/container\", ...]\n"
"console.log(JSON.parse(await getAvailableBackends()));              // "
"BackendInfo[] — full probe\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"import {\n"
"  setBackend, setBackends, getBackend, getBackendPriority,\n"
"  getAvailableBackends, selectBackendFor, up,\n"
"} from 'perry/container';\n"
"\n"
"// (3a) Pin a specific backend for everything in this process.\n"
"await setBackend('docker');\n"
"\n"
"// (3b) Or — try a list in user-defined priority order (first\n"
"//      available wins). Useful for \"prefer rootless, fall back to\n"
"//      docker\" patterns and CI matrix lanes.\n"
"await setBackends(['podman', 'docker']);\n"
"\n"
"// (4) Or — let Perry pick the best backend FOR THIS SPEC.\n"
"//     Spec uses privileged: true → returns \"docker\" / \"podman\" (not "
"apple).\n"
"//     Trivial spec on macOS → returns \"apple/container\".\n"
"const best = JSON.parse(selectBackendFor(JSON.stringify(spec))) as string;\n"
"await setBackend(best);\n"
"await up(spec);\n"
"\n"
"// Diagnostics — which backends does Perry know about, and which are\n"
"// actually installed on this host?\n"
"console.log(getBackend());                                          // "
"\"docker\" (active)\n"
"console.log(JSON.parse(getBackendPriority()));                      // "
"[\"apple/container\", ...]\n"
"console.log(JSON.parse(await getAvailableBackends()));              // "
"BackendInfo[] — full probe\n"
"```"

#: src/container/overview.md:104
msgid ""
"`setBackend()` rejects after the first container op fires — the global "
"backend `OnceLock` can't be reset. Set it before any other `perry/container` "
"or `perry/compose` call. See [Cross-Backend Determinism](./determinism.md) "
"for the full architecture and the capability-aware `selectBackendFor()` "
"semantics."
msgstr ""
"`setBackend()` rechaza después de que se dispara la primera operación de "
"contenedor — el `OnceLock` del backend global no puede reiniciarse. "
"Configúrelo antes de cualquier otra llamada a `perry/container` o `perry/"
"compose`. Consulte [Determinismo entre backends](./determinism.md) para la "
"arquitectura completa y la semántica de `selectBackendFor()` con conciencia "
"de capacidades."

#: src/container/overview.md:110 src/cli/updates.md:142
msgid "Environment variables"
msgstr "Variables de entorno"

#: src/container/overview.md:114
msgid "`PERRY_CONTAINER_BACKEND=<name>`"
msgstr "`PERRY_CONTAINER_BACKEND=<name>`"

#: src/container/overview.md:114
msgid ""
"Process-level backend pin (skips auto-detection). Same effect as calling "
"`setBackend(name)` from TS, but works before the first op fires. Errors with "
"`NoBackendFound` if the named backend isn't probeable."
msgstr ""
"Pin del backend a nivel de proceso (omite la auto-detección). Tiene el mismo "
"efecto que llamar a `setBackend(name)` desde TS, pero funciona antes de que "
"se dispare la primera operación. Produce un error `NoBackendFound` si el "
"backend indicado no puede ser sondeado."

#: src/container/overview.md:115
msgid "`PERRY_NO_INSTALL_PROMPT=1`"
msgstr "`PERRY_NO_INSTALL_PROMPT=1`"

#: src/container/overview.md:115
msgid ""
"Disable the interactive installer when no backend is found. Defaults to "
"allowed when `stderr` is a TTY."
msgstr ""
"Deshabilita el instalador interactivo cuando no se encuentra ningún backend. "
"Por defecto está permitido cuando `stderr` es un TTY."

#: src/container/overview.md:116
msgid "`PERRY_CONTAINER_VERIFY_IMAGES=1`"
msgstr "`PERRY_CONTAINER_VERIFY_IMAGES=1`"

#: src/container/overview.md:116
msgid ""
"Run `cosign verify` against every pulled image before use. See [Security](./"
"security.md#image-verification)."
msgstr ""
"Ejecuta `cosign verify` contra cada imagen descargada antes de usarla. "
"Consulte [Seguridad](./security.md#image-verification)."

#: src/container/overview.md:117
msgid "`PERRY_ALLOW_UNTRUSTED_SHARED_KERNEL=1`"
msgstr "`PERRY_ALLOW_UNTRUSTED_SHARED_KERNEL=1`"

#: src/container/overview.md:117
msgid ""
"Opt out of the workload-graph requirement that `policy.tier = \"untrusted\"` "
"runs in a microVM. **Not recommended for actual untrusted code.**"
msgstr ""
"Permite omitir el requisito del grafo de cargas de trabajo de que "
"`policy.tier = \"untrusted\"` se ejecute en una microVM. **No se recomienda "
"para código realmente no confiable.**"

#: src/container/overview.md:118
msgid "`PERRY_NO_DEFAULT_SIGINT_CLEANUP=1`"
msgstr "`PERRY_NO_DEFAULT_SIGINT_CLEANUP=1`"

#: src/container/overview.md:118
msgid ""
"Skip the default SIGINT/SIGTERM handler that drains `COMPOSE_HANDLES`. Tests "
"+ tools that own their own teardown set this."
msgstr ""
"Omite el manejador predeterminado de SIGINT/SIGTERM que drena "
"`COMPOSE_HANDLES`. Tests y herramientas que gestionan su propio desmontaje "
"deben configurar esto."

#: src/container/overview.md:120
msgid "Module layout"
msgstr "Estructura de módulos"

#: src/container/overview.md:137
msgid ""
"The split exists so the compiler can stay agnostic about which runtime will "
"actually execute the spec: HIR + codegen reference symbol _strings_ only, "
"and the runtime backend is swappable without recompilation of user code."
msgstr ""
"La división existe para que el compiler pueda mantenerse agnóstico sobre qué "
"runtime ejecutará realmente la especificación: HIR + codegen referencian "
"únicamente _cadenas_ de símbolos, y el backend del runtime es intercambiable "
"sin recompilar el código del usuario."

#: src/container/overview.md:142
msgid "Canonical lifecycle"
msgstr "Ciclo de vida canónico"

#: src/container/overview.md:144
msgid ""
"The pattern most production deployments follow is the same as `docker "
"compose up -d` / `down`:"
msgstr ""
"El patrón que sigue la mayoría de los despliegues en producción es el mismo "
"que `docker compose up -d` / `down`:"

#: src/container/overview.md:147
msgid ""
"**`up()`** — bring the stack up, return an opaque integer handle, and exit "
"when every service is started (`up()` does not block on healthchecks; for "
"that, see [Healthchecks & readiness](./compose.md#waiting-for-readiness))."
msgstr ""
"**`up()`** — levanta el stack, devuelve un identificador entero opaco y "
"termina cuando todos los servicios han arrancado (`up()` no bloquea en los "
"healthchecks; para eso, consulte [Healthchecks y disponibilidad](./"
"compose.md#waiting-for-readiness))."

#: src/container/overview.md:151
msgid ""
"**Run a separate readiness probe** (or rely on the in-spec `healthcheck` "
"block) to verify the stack is actually serving."
msgstr ""
"**Ejecute una sonda de disponibilidad separada** (o confíe en el bloque "
"`healthcheck` de la especificación) para verificar que el stack realmente "
"está sirviendo."

#: src/container/overview.md:153
msgid ""
"**Exit 0**: the containers keep running thanks to docker's daemon (`restart: "
"unless-stopped` survives host reboots)."
msgstr ""
"**Salida 0**: los contenedores continúan ejecutándose gracias al daemon de "
"docker (`restart: unless-stopped` sobrevive reinicios del host)."

#: src/container/overview.md:155
msgid ""
"**`down(handle)`** later (typically from a separate invocation) to tear the "
"stack down. Volumes are preserved by default; pass `{ volumes: true }` to "
"also drop them."
msgstr ""
"**`down(handle)`** más adelante (típicamente desde una invocación separada) "
"para desmontar el stack. Los volúmenes se conservan por defecto; pase "
"`{ volumes: true }` para eliminarlos también."

#: src/container/overview.md:159
msgid ""
"Perry's runtime currently does not deliver `process.on('SIGINT', ...)` "
"handlers to your TS code, so a `Ctrl-C`\\-tears-down pattern can't be "
"written today. The example deployments under [`example-code/forgejo-"
"deployment`](https://github.com/PerryTS/perry/tree/main/example-code/forgejo-"
"deployment) use the two-invocation pattern (`./forgejo_app` and `./"
"forgejo_app --down`) instead."
msgstr ""
"El runtime de Perry actualmente no entrega manejadores "
"`process.on('SIGINT', ...)` al código TS, por lo que hoy no es posible "
"escribir un patrón de desmontaje con `Ctrl-C`. Los ejemplos de despliegue en "
"[`example-code/forgejo-deployment`](https://github.com/PerryTS/perry/tree/"
"main/example-code/forgejo-deployment) utilizan en su lugar el patrón de dos "
"invocaciones (`./forgejo_app` y `./forgejo_app --down`)."

