#: src/container/compose.md:1
msgid "Compose Orchestration (`perry/compose`)"
msgstr "Orquestación con Compose (`perry/compose`)"

#: src/container/compose.md:3
msgid ""
"`perry/compose` brings the `docker compose up / down / ps / exec / logs` "
"workflow into TypeScript. The spec is a TS object literal that mirrors the "
"[Compose Specification](https://github.com/compose-spec/compose-spec/blob/"
"main/schema/compose-spec.json), the engine is in-process Rust (no shell-out "
"to a `docker-compose` binary), and dependency ordering / rollback / "
"interpolation all run natively."
msgstr ""
"`perry/compose` integra el flujo de trabajo `docker compose up / down / ps / "
"exec / logs` en TypeScript. La especificación es un objeto literal de TS que "
"refleja la [Compose Specification](https://github.com/compose-spec/compose-"
"spec/blob/main/schema/compose-spec.json), el motor es Rust en proceso (sin "
"llamadas al shell a un binario `docker-compose`), y el ordenamiento de "
"dependencias, el rollback y la interpolación se ejecutan de forma nativa."

#: src/container/compose.md:10
msgid "Bringing up a single-service stack"
msgstr "Levantar una pila de un solo servicio"

#: src/container/compose.md:41
msgid ""
"The handle returned from `up()` is an opaque integer (NaN-boxed with "
"`POINTER_TAG`); pass it as the first argument to [`down`](#tearing-down) / "
"[`ps`](#status--logs--exec) / [`logs`](#status--logs--exec) / [`exec`]"
"(#status--logs--exec). The template-string interpolation `${stack}` renders "
"as `[object Object]` because of the NaN-boxing tag; coerce explicitly with "
"`String(stack)` if you need to log it."
msgstr ""
"El identificador devuelto por `up()` es un entero opaco (NaN-boxed con "
"`POINTER_TAG`); pásalo como primer argumento a [`down`](#tearing-down) / "
"[`ps`](#status--logs--exec) / [`logs`](#status--logs--exec) / [`exec`]"
"(#status--logs--exec). La interpolación de cadenas de plantilla `${stack}` "
"se renderiza como `[object Object]` debido a la etiqueta de NaN-boxing; "
"conviértelo explícitamente con `String(stack)` si necesitas registrarlo."

#: src/container/compose.md:49
msgid "Multi-service stack with healthcheck-gated startup"
msgstr "Pila de múltiples servicios con inicio controlado por healthcheck"

#: src/container/compose.md:51
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"import { up as upMulti } from \"perry/compose\";\n"
"\n"
"async function bringUpMultiServiceStack(): Promise<void> {\n"
"    // depends_on with `condition: 'service_healthy'` blocks the\n"
"    // dependent service until the dependency's healthcheck reports\n"
"    // healthy. Use the map form (not the bare-array form) to pass\n"
"    // the condition.\n"
"    await upMulti({\n"
"        version: \"3.8\",\n"
"        services: {\n"
"            db: {\n"
"                image: \"postgres:16-alpine\",\n"
"                container_name: \"app-db\", // stable DNS target for "
"siblings\n"
"                environment: {\n"
"                    POSTGRES_USER:     \"app\",\n"
"                    POSTGRES_PASSWORD: \"${APP_DB_PASSWORD:-changeme}\",\n"
"                    POSTGRES_DB:       \"app\",\n"
"                },\n"
"                volumes: [\"app-pgdata:/var/lib/postgresql/data\"],\n"
"                networks: [\"app-db-net\"],\n"
"                healthcheck: {\n"
"                    test: [\"CMD-SHELL\", \"pg_isready -U app -d app\"],\n"
"                    interval: \"5s\",\n"
"                    timeout: \"3s\",\n"
"                    retries: 10,\n"
"                    start_period: \"30s\",\n"
"                },\n"
"            },\n"
"            api: {\n"
"                image: \"myorg/api:1.0\",\n"
"                depends_on: { db: { condition: \"service_healthy\" } },\n"
"                environment: {\n"
"                    DATABASE_URL: \"postgres://app:changeme@app-db:5432/"
"app\",\n"
"                },\n"
"                ports: [\"8080:8080\"],\n"
"                networks: [\"app-db-net\", \"app-web-net\"],\n"
"                restart: \"unless-stopped\",\n"
"            },\n"
"        },\n"
"        networks: {\n"
"            \"app-db-net\":  { driver: \"bridge\", internal: true }, // db "
"unreachable from host\n"
"            \"app-web-net\": { driver: \"bridge\" },\n"
"        },\n"
"        volumes: {\n"
"            \"app-pgdata\": { driver: \"local\" },\n"
"        },\n"
"    });\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"import { up as upMulti } from \"perry/compose\";\n"
"\n"
"async function bringUpMultiServiceStack(): Promise<void> {\n"
"    // depends_on with `condition: 'service_healthy'` blocks the\n"
"    // dependent service until the dependency's healthcheck reports\n"
"    // healthy. Use the map form (not the bare-array form) to pass\n"
"    // the condition.\n"
"    await upMulti({\n"
"        version: \"3.8\",\n"
"        services: {\n"
"            db: {\n"
"                image: \"postgres:16-alpine\",\n"
"                container_name: \"app-db\", // stable DNS target for "
"siblings\n"
"                environment: {\n"
"                    POSTGRES_USER:     \"app\",\n"
"                    POSTGRES_PASSWORD: \"${APP_DB_PASSWORD:-changeme}\",\n"
"                    POSTGRES_DB:       \"app\",\n"
"                },\n"
"                volumes: [\"app-pgdata:/var/lib/postgresql/data\"],\n"
"                networks: [\"app-db-net\"],\n"
"                healthcheck: {\n"
"                    test: [\"CMD-SHELL\", \"pg_isready -U app -d app\"],\n"
"                    interval: \"5s\",\n"
"                    timeout: \"3s\",\n"
"                    retries: 10,\n"
"                    start_period: \"30s\",\n"
"                },\n"
"            },\n"
"            api: {\n"
"                image: \"myorg/api:1.0\",\n"
"                depends_on: { db: { condition: \"service_healthy\" } },\n"
"                environment: {\n"
"                    DATABASE_URL: \"postgres://app:changeme@app-db:5432/"
"app\",\n"
"                },\n"
"                ports: [\"8080:8080\"],\n"
"                networks: [\"app-db-net\", \"app-web-net\"],\n"
"                restart: \"unless-stopped\",\n"
"            },\n"
"        },\n"
"        networks: {\n"
"            \"app-db-net\":  { driver: \"bridge\", internal: true }, // db "
"unreachable from host\n"
"            \"app-web-net\": { driver: \"bridge\" },\n"
"        },\n"
"        volumes: {\n"
"            \"app-pgdata\": { driver: \"local\" },\n"
"        },\n"
"    });\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/container/compose.md:102
msgid "This pattern combines several production-grade primitives:"
msgstr "Este patrón combina varios primitivos de nivel de producción:"

#: src/container/compose.md:104
msgid "Primitive"
msgstr "Primitivo"

#: src/container/compose.md:106
msgid "`container_name: 'app-db'`"
msgstr "`container_name: 'app-db'`"

#: src/container/compose.md:106
msgid ""
"Forces a stable container name so docker's embedded DNS resolves `app-db` to "
"the postgres container's IP. **See the [DNS gotcha below](#cross-service-"
"dns).**"
msgstr ""
"Forza un nombre de contenedor estable así que el DNS integrado de Docker "
"resuelve `app-db` a la IP del contenedor postgres. **Ver el [DNS te tiene "
"abajo](#cross-service-dns).**"

#: src/container/compose.md:107
msgid "`healthcheck: { test: [...], interval, retries, start_period }`"
msgstr "`healthcheck: { test: [...], interval, retries, start_period }`"

#: src/container/compose.md:107
msgid ""
"Per-service liveness probe. Compose-spec § service.healthcheck shape — "
"Perry's engine honors it for `depends_on` gating."
msgstr ""
"Sonda de vida por servicio. Compuesta-espec § service.healthcheck forma — "
"Perry el motor lo honra por `depends_on` gating."

#: src/container/compose.md:108
msgid "`depends_on: { db: { condition: 'service_healthy' } }`"
msgstr "`depends_on: { db: { condition: 'service_healthy' } }`"

#: src/container/compose.md:108
msgid ""
"Holds the dependent service back until the dependency reports healthy. Three "
"valid conditions: `service_started`, `service_healthy`, "
"`service_completed_successfully`."
msgstr ""
"Retiene el servicio dependiente hasta que la dependencia reporta estado "
"saludable. Tres condiciones válidas: `service_started`, `service_healthy`, "
"`service_completed_successfully`."

#: src/container/compose.md:109
msgid "`networks: { ..., internal: true }`"
msgstr "`networks: { ..., internal: true }`"

#: src/container/compose.md:109
msgid ""
"Marks the network as internal-only — postgres is unreachable from the host "
"or from sibling stacks. See [Networking](./networking.md)."
msgstr ""
"Marca la red como solo interna — postgres no es accesible desde el host ni "
"desde stacks hermanos. Consulta [Redes](./networking.md)."

#: src/container/compose.md:110
msgid "`restart: 'unless-stopped'`"
msgstr "`restart: 'unless-stopped'`"

#: src/container/compose.md:110
msgid ""
"The runtime restarts the container after a crash, but not after an explicit "
"`docker stop`."
msgstr ""
"El runtime reinicia el contenedor tras un fallo, pero no tras un `docker "
"stop` explícito."

#: src/container/compose.md:112
msgid ""
"The full `ComposeSpec` shape is exported from `perry/compose` as "
"`ComposeSpec`, with sub-types `Service`, `ComposeNetwork`, `ComposeVolume`, "
"`Build`, and `Healthcheck`."
msgstr ""
"La forma completa de `ComposeSpec` se exporta desde `perry/compose` como "
"`ComposeSpec`, con los subtipos `Service`, `ComposeNetwork`, "
"`ComposeVolume`, `Build` y `Healthcheck`."

#: src/container/compose.md:116
msgid ""
"The root-level `name:` field sets the **compose project name** — it labels "
"every container (`perry.compose.project=<name>`) and namespaces non-external "
"volumes and networks as `<name>_<declared-name>`, exactly like docker-"
"compose's project prefix. It defaults to `\"perry-stack\"` when omitted, so "
"set it whenever more than one stack can run on the same host (see [Volumes → "
"Volume naming and ownership](./volumes.md#volume-naming-and-ownership))."
msgstr ""
"El campo `name:` de nivel raíz establece el **componer el nombre del "
"proyecto** — etiqueta cada contenedor (`perry.compose.project=<name>`) y los "
"espacios de nombres de volúmenes y redes no externos como `<name>_<declared-"
"name>`, exactamente igual que el prefijo de proyecto de docker-compose. Por "
"defecto, `\"perry-stack\"` se omite, así que configúralo siempre que más de "
"una pila se pueda ejecutar en el mismo host (véase [Volúmenes → Nombre de "
"volumen y propiedad](./volumes.md#volume-naming-and-ownership))."

