msgid "Range mapping (UDP/TCP, host:container both inclusive)."
msgstr "Mapeo de rango (UDP/TCP, host:contenedor ambos inclusive)."

#: src/container/networking.md:143
msgid ""
"For services that should never be host-published (private databases, "
"internal-only side-cars), simply **don't list any ports**. Combined with "
"`internal: true` on the network, those services are unreachable from the "
"host even if a port slipped into the spec by mistake."
msgstr ""
"Para los servicios que nunca deben publicarse en el host (bases de datos "
"privadas, sidecars de uso interno), simplemente **no liste ningún puerto**. "
"Combinado con `internal: true` en la red, esos servicios son inalcanzables "
"desde el host aunque un puerto se haya colado en la especificación por error."

#: src/container/networking.md:148
msgid "Single-network shorthand"
msgstr "Atajo de red única"

#: src/container/networking.md:150
msgid ""
"When every service joins the same network, you can put `networks:  "
"['<name>']` on each service and `networks: { <name>: {...} }` once at the "
"root. The engine deduplicates network creation across services."
msgstr ""
"Cuando cada servicio se une a la misma red, puede poner `networks:  "
"['<name>']` en cada servicio y `networks: { <name>: {...} }` una vez en el "
"root. El motor deduplica la creación de red entre los servicios."

#: src/container/networking.md:154
msgid "Networks created in this session vs. external"
msgstr "Redes creadas en esta sesión vs. externas"

#: src/container/networking.md:156
msgid ""
"Perry tracks **session networks** (created during this `up()` call) and "
"distinguishes them from `external: true` networks (assumed pre-existing and "
"shared across stacks). On `down()`, only session networks are torn down — "
"external networks are left alone, matching docker-compose semantics."
msgstr ""
"Perry hace seguimiento de las **redes de sesión** (creadas durante esta "
"llamada a `up()`) y las distingue de las redes con `external: true` (se "
"asume que ya existen y son compartidas entre stacks). En `down()`, solo se "
"eliminan las redes de sesión — las redes externas se dejan intactas, "
"siguiendo la semántica de docker-compose."

#: src/container/networking.md:162
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"networks: {\n"
"  // Session: created if missing; removed on down()\n"
"  \"app-net\": { driver: \"bridge\" },\n"
"\n"
"  // External: must already exist; never touched on down()\n"
"  \"shared-public-net\": { external: true, name: \"external_pub_v1\" },\n"
"},\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"networks: {\n"
"  // Session: created if missing; removed on down()\n"
"  \"app-net\": { driver: \"bridge\" },\n"
"\n"
"  // External: must already exist; never touched on down()\n"
"  \"shared-public-net\": { external: true, name: \"external_pub_v1\" },\n"
"},\n"
"```"

