"│   └── index.ts              # TypeScript API (what users import)\n"
"├── crate-ios/                # iOS/macOS native implementation\n"
"│   ├── Cargo.toml            # [lib] crate-type = [\"staticlib\"]\n"
"│   ├── build.rs              # Compiles Swift if needed\n"
"│   ├── src/\n"
"│   │   └── lib.rs            # Rust FFI: #[no_mangle] pub extern \"C\" "
"fn ...\n"
"│   └── swift/\n"
"│       └── bridge.swift      # Swift bridge for Apple APIs (@_cdecl)\n"
"├── crate-android/            # Android native implementation\n"
"│   ├── Cargo.toml\n"
"│   └── src/\n"
"│       └── lib.rs            # Rust FFI with JNI calls\n"
"└── crate-stub/               # Fallback for unsupported platforms\n"
"    ├── Cargo.toml\n"
"    └── src/\n"
"        └── lib.rs            # Returns error immediately\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```\n"
"perry-appstore-review/\n"
"├── package.json              # Manifest with perry.nativeLibrary\n"
"├── src/\n"
"│   └── index.ts              # TypeScript API (what users import)\n"
"├── crate-ios/                # iOS/macOS native implementation\n"
"│   ├── Cargo.toml            # [lib] crate-type = [\"staticlib\"]\n"
"│   ├── build.rs              # Compiles Swift if needed\n"
"│   ├── src/\n"
"│   │   └── lib.rs            # Rust FFI: #[no_mangle] pub extern \"C\" "
"fn ...\n"
"│   └── swift/\n"
"│       └── bridge.swift      # Swift bridge for Apple APIs (@_cdecl)\n"
"├── crate-android/            # Android native implementation\n"
"│   ├── Cargo.toml\n"
"│   └── src/\n"
"│       └── lib.rs            # Rust FFI with JNI calls\n"
"└── crate-stub/               # Fallback for unsupported platforms\n"
"    ├── Cargo.toml\n"
"    └── src/\n"
"        └── lib.rs            # Returns error immediately\n"
"```"

#: src/plugins/native-extensions.md:134
msgid "TypeScript side"
msgstr "Lado de TypeScript"

#: src/plugins/native-extensions.md:136
msgid ""
"The `src/index.ts` declares native functions and optionally wraps them in a "
"friendlier API:"
msgstr ""
"El archivo `src/index.ts` declara las funciones nativas y opcionalmente las "
"envuelve en una API más amigable:"

#: src/plugins/native-extensions.md:138
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"// Declare the native function (name must match package.json)\n"
"declare function sb_appreview_request(): number;\n"
"\n"
"// Wrap it with a proper TypeScript signature\n"
"export async function requestReview(): Promise<void> {\n"
"  await (sb_appreview_request() as any);\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"// Declare the native function (name must match package.json)\n"
"declare function sb_appreview_request(): number;\n"
"\n"
"// Wrap it with a proper TypeScript signature\n"
"export async function requestReview(): Promise<void> {\n"
"  await (sb_appreview_request() as any);\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/plugins/native-extensions.md:148
msgid ""
"`declare function` tells Perry the function is provided by native code. The "
"raw return type is `number` because all values cross the FFI boundary as NaN-"
"boxed `f64` values. Promise handles are NaN-boxed pointers that Perry's "
"runtime knows how to `await`."
msgstr ""
"`declare function` le indica a Perry que la función es provista por código "
"nativo. El tipo de retorno crudo es `number` porque todos los valores cruzan "
"el límite FFI como valores `f64` con NaN-boxing. Los handles de Promise son "
"punteros con NaN-boxing que el runtime de Perry sabe cómo manejar con "
"`await`."

#: src/plugins/native-extensions.md:150
msgid "Ergonomic aliases and the wrapper-name collision rule"
msgstr "Alias ergonómicos y regla de colisión de nombre de envoltorio"

#: src/plugins/native-extensions.md:152
msgid ""
"For manifest symbols that follow the `js_<pkg>_<snake_case>` convention "
"(where `<pkg>` is the sanitized last segment of the package name), Perry "
"derives an **ergonomic camelCase alias** so consumers can import a spec-"
"faithful name without you writing any wrapper (issue #5621). For `@perryts/"
"webgpu` a manifest symbol `js_webgpu_request_adapter` is importable as "
"`requestAdapter`:"
msgstr ""
"Para los símbolos manifiestos que siguen la convención "
"`js_<pkg>_<snake_case>` (donde `<pkg>` es el último segmento desinfectado "
"del nombre del paquete), Perry deriva un **alias ergonómico camelCase** para "
"que los consumidores puedan importar un nombre fiel a las especificaciones "
"sin que usted escriba ningún envoltorio (tema #5621). Para `@perryts/webgpu` "
"un símbolo de manifiesto `js_webgpu_request_adapter` es importable como "
"`requestAdapter`:"

#: src/plugins/native-extensions.md:154
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"// The package's src/index.ts only ambient-declares the raw symbols…\n"
"export declare function js_webgpu_request_adapter(): Promise<number>;\n"
"\n"
"// …and consumers import the derived alias:\n"
"import { requestAdapter } from \"@perryts/webgpu\"; // → "
"js_webgpu_request_adapter\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"// The package's src/index.ts only ambient-declares the raw symbols…\n"
"export declare function js_webgpu_request_adapter(): Promise<number>;\n"
"\n"
"// …and consumers import the derived alias:\n"
"import { requestAdapter } from \"@perryts/webgpu\"; // → "
"js_webgpu_request_adapter\n"
"```"

#: src/plugins/native-extensions.md:162
msgid ""
"The alias is a convenience **for packages that only export ambient `declare` "
"signatures**. A _genuine_ implemented export always wins over a derived "
"alias (issue #6715): if your `src/index.ts` also exports a real wrapper "
"whose name equals a manifest symbol's derived alias, the import binds to "
"**your wrapper**, not the FFI symbol — your wrapper code runs, and it can "
"call the raw symbol internally:"
msgstr ""
"El alias es una conveniencia **para paquetes que solo exportan firmas "
"`declare` ambientales**. Una exportación _genuine_ implementada siempre gana "
"sobre un alias derivado (emisión #6715): si su `src/index.ts` también "
"exporta un envoltorio real cuyo nombre es igual al alias derivado de un "
"símbolo manifiesto, la importación se une a **su envoltura**, no el símbolo "
"FFI — su código de envoltura se ejecuta, y puede llamar al símbolo en bruto "
"internamente:"

#: src/plugins/native-extensions.md:164
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"export declare function js_speech_speak(\n"
"  text: string, rate: number, pitch: number, locale: string, voiceId: "
"string): Promise<number>;\n"
"\n"
"// `speak` is the derived alias of `js_speech_speak` — this real wrapper "
"WINS.\n"
"export async function speak(text: string, options?: { rate?: number }): "
"Promise<boolean> {\n"
"  const rate = options?.rate ?? -1;\n"
"  return (await js_speech_speak(text, rate, -1, \"\", \"\")) !== 0;\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"export declare function js_speech_speak(\n"
"  text: string, rate: number, pitch: number, locale: string, voiceId: "
"string): Promise<number>;\n"
"\n"
"// `speak` is the derived alias of `js_speech_speak` — this real wrapper "
"WINS.\n"
"export async function speak(text: string, options?: { rate?: number }): "
"Promise<boolean> {\n"
"  const rate = options?.rate ?? -1;\n"
"  return (await js_speech_speak(text, rate, -1, \"\", \"\")) !== 0;\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/plugins/native-extensions.md:175
msgid ""
"**Recommended convention.** If you write real wrapper logic (options "
"objects, JSON parsing, bool coercion) around your externs, name the manifest "
"symbols `js_<pkg>_native_<snake>` so their derived aliases become "
"`nativeSpeak`, `nativeDoThing`, etc. — names your package simply doesn't re-"
"export. This keeps the aliases out of your public namespace and removes any "
"chance of a wrapper/alias name clash. If two manifest symbols ever derive "
"the _same_ alias, Perry reports a hard compile error rather than binding to "
"one silently."
msgstr ""
"**Convención recomendada.** Si escribes una lógica de envoltura real "
"(opciones de objetos, análisis de JSON, coacción bool) alrededor de tus "
"externas, nombra los símbolos manifiestos `js_<pkg>_native_<snake>` para que "
"sus alias derivados se conviertan en `nativeSpeak`, `nativeDoThing`, etc. — "
"nombra tu paquete simplemente no reexporta. Esto mantiene los alias fuera de "
"su espacio de nombres públicos y elimina cualquier posibilidad de un choque "
"de nombre wrapper/alias. Si dos símbolos manifiestos alguna vez derivan el "
"alias _same_, Perry informa de un error de compilación difícil en lugar de "
"unirse a uno silenciosamente."

